# cause: an unescaped pipe adds a body cell

Header and delimiter agree at 2. The body row has 4, because the unescaped
pipes inside the code span split it at BLOCK level, before inline parsing.
GFM still renders a table and silently DROPS the excess.

EXPECT: markdownlint HIT (MD056), rumdl SILENT.

This is the state a formatter can escalate: prettier 3.8.3 widened the
delimiter row to match the widest row, turning this into the break above.

| A | B |
| - | - |
| x | `|| true` y |
